+<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Neural kernel conformance</title><style>body{max-width:960px;margin:40px auto;font:16px system-ui;line-height:1.5;padding:16px}pre{white-space:pre-wrap;background:#eee;padding:16px}button{padding:10px}</style><h1>Compact neural kernel conformance</h1><p>This runs the shipped WebGPU kernels against independent PyTorch fixtures. The fixture weights are untrained. Passing proves mathematical agreement within a tolerance, not good interpolation quality or real-time performance.</p><p>Serve the source directory locally: <code>python -m http.server 8765 --bind 127.0.0.1</code>, then open <code>http://localhost:8765/test/neural-conformance.html</code> in the target browser. No runtime code or video leaves the machine.</p><button id="run">Run WebGPU conformance</button><pre id="log">Ready</pre><script src="../fi-quality.js"></script><script src="../fi-neural-runtime.js"></script><script src="neural-conformance.js"></script></html>
